Experimental startup managed timer exclusion; not automatically applied by Context Foundry.
Target: can1357/oh-my-pi @ 24439066040e006eb08da7b204f0ac41c79d2de9
Owner: 003 T006 bounded-pilot-v2 startup observation and admission.
Requires prior caller/auth/refusal/restricted/catalog/settings/empty-auth/presence/telemetry/marketplace/logging/plugin-roots/extension patches.
Modules: extensions/managed-timers::{setTimeout,setInterval,excludeStartupManagedTimers}; extensions/runner::ownStartupExtension.
Tests: startup-extension-owner.test.ts and existing extensions-runner, SDK and CLI suites.
Difference: the restricted startup extension owner refuses installation after any
managed timer start and rejects managed timeout/interval before handle construction.
Ordinary managed timers remain available without the owner. Raw timers, arbitrary
extension work, complete inventory, Ready, paid execution, signing and release remain open.

